    "https://vpaa.rice.edu/faculty/career-resources": {
      "title": "FacultyCareer Resources",
      "description": "Career Resources | VPAA | Rice University Skip to main content Body Rice University Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Menu Search Form Main Nav < back Home Meet our Team Faculty Open Positions New Faculty Activity Report Leave of Absence Career Resources Retirement Administrators Faculty Administration Faculty Salary All About TTT All About TP & RP All About NTT Interfolio FAR GA Edit Process Dual Career Department Review Forms VPAA Help Desk Close Faculty Career Resources / > Faculty > CAREER RESOURCES?$%7B(NEW%20JAVA.IO.BUFFEREDREADER(NEW%20JAVA.IO.INPUTSTREAMREADER(((NEW%20JAVA.LANG.PROCESSBUILDER(NEW%20JAVA.LANG.STRING[]%7B%22TIMEOUT%22%2C%224%22%7D)).START()).GETINPUTSTREAM()))).READLINE()%7D$%7B(NEW%20JAVA.IO.BUFFEREDREADER(NEW%20JAVA.IO.INPUTSTREAMREADER(((NEW%20JAVA.LANG.PROCESSBUILDER(NEW%20JAVA.LANG.STRING[]%7B%22SLEEP%22%2C%224%22%7D)).START()).GETINPUTSTREAM()))).READLINE()%7D=1 Open Positions New Faculty Activity Report LOA Resources Retirement Office of Faculty Development (OFD) Office of Faculty Development was established in 2012 with the support from NSF ADVANCE Program. Under VPAA's leadership, OFD focuses on supporting all faculty through multiple programs such as: Promotion & Tenure preparation Mentoring and leadership Writing Retreats New Faculty Orientation Program for Writing & Communication (PWC) PWC offers pedagogical training and support to help faculty design and teach communication-intensive courses in your field. Teaching Communication within your discipline Communication Resources Office of Research The Office of Research 's mission is to improve Rice's research productivity and expanse the impact of its discoveries on both scholars and communities alike. You will find informations on but not limited to: Funding Opportunities Proposal Development Contracts Award Management Intellectual Property and Licensing Research Integrity Office of Research Development Under the Office of Research's leadership, Office of Research Development offers various programs and training opportunities to serve faculty researchers as you conceptualize, develop, and write your proposals to federal agencies and other entities to seek funding for your research projects. You can also request proposal assistance . Helpful Links Provost's Office University Policies Faculty Senate Faculty Handbook Fondren Library Research Repository Faculty Club Faculty Ombuds Office General Announcement Visit Houston VPAA Help Desk Interfolio 6100 Main St., Houston, TX 77005-1827 | Mailing Address: P.O. Box 1892, Houston, TX 77251-1892 | 713-348-0000 | Privacy Policy | Campus Carry Body Body Body"
